    "summaries": [
      {
        "action_date": "2025-03-25",
        "action_desc": "Introduced in House",
        "text": "<p><strong>John W. Walsh Alpha-1 Home Infusion Act of 2025</strong><strong></strong></p><p>This bill provides for Medicare coverage of treatment for alpha-1 antitrypsin (AAT) deficiency (a protein deficiency that raises the risk of lung and other diseases). Specifically, the bill provides for coverage of at-home augmentation therapy for beneficiaries with emphysema as a result of severe hereditary AAT deficiency. Treatment must be provided through qualified home infusion therapy suppliers; beneficiaries must be under the care of a physician, nurse practitioner, or physician assistant.</p>",
        "update_date": "2025-04-18T17:27:26Z"
      }
    ]
  },
